  "bug_description": "### 🐛 Describe the bug\n\nCalling torch.fmod on int64 tensors crashes the Python process (segfault / arithmetic exception) when any element satisfies a == INT64_MIN and b == -1.\n```python\nimport torch\n\ndividend = torch.full((2, 3), torch.iinfo(torch.int64).min, dtype=torch.int64, device='cpu')\ndivisor = torch.full((3,), -1, dtype=torch.int64, device='cpu')\n\nprint(\"Dividend tensor:\", dividend)\nprint(\"Divisor tensor:\", divisor)\n\nresult = torch.fmod(dividend, divisor)\nprint(\"Result:\", result)\n```\n\n\n### Versions\n\n```\nPyTorch version: 2.5.1+cu124\n```\n\ncc @albanD",
